# The own pass's findings in std's own functions that tests/std/own.sh
# accepts: `CODE ITEM  why`. Each is a false positive of the pass's
# conservative origins, with the reason no view outlives or is invalidated
# under what it views (0.25 audit: each entry checked against the code;
# none hides a summary callers use: they see the inferred or pinned one,
# which over-approximates); remove a line once the pass or std changes
# (own.sh notes a line no longer found).
own.conflict std::Buf::push_fmt  sound: f (__buf_fmt(&self)) is the only path to self until __buf_fmt_end(&self, &f) consumes it, and it only commits f's length; nothing else touches self between them
own.conflict std::string::String::push_fmt  sound: the same, into the String's bytes
own.conflict std::fmt::format_in  sound: the same Fmt design: f is the only path to b's room; __fmt_in_end(&b, &f, &tmp) grows b and points f at its new room in one call, and x.fmt writes only through f; b is not used otherwise until it is returned
own.conflict std::collections::raw_table::RawTable::probe_stats  sound: self is a let borrow, so nothing writes the table while it is iterated; hasher only reads the element it is given (tests only)
own.escape std::Vec::sort_by_key  sound: the sort permutes s's own elements through raw pointers; is_less (whose view of g is the finding) only compares and stores nothing; the escape comes from the generic floor's stores (an inout parameter may gain any argument's T values)
own.escape std::slice::sort_stable_by_in  sound: the same
own.escape std::collections::hash_map::HashMap::raw_table  sound: a `-> let T` result (a projection) is reported as unsupported, but callers use the pin #[views(self)], which holds (the result points into self's table)
own.escape std::collections::raw_table::RawTable::get  sound: the same, #[views(self)] of a bucket of self
own.conflict std::gpu::wgsl::msl::W::struct_def  sound: b is a local Buf that push_fmt copies bytes into; nm(self.pool, ..) is read before self.member_ty changes the pool, and b keeps no view of it (the floor's stores of Buf<ScopedArena>::push_str say it may)
own.conflict std::gpu::wgsl::msl::write_entry  sound: w.intern copies into w.pool; in_buf is a separate local Buf, viewed by nothing in w (the same floor stores)
own.escape std::gpu::wgsl::msl::W::image_load  sound: push_fmt into a Buf<ScopedArena> copies the bytes; the floor's stores of the arena-viewing Buf take it as keeping a view of lb
own.escape std::gpu::wgsl::msl::W::lit  sound: self.p(s) copies s's bytes into self.out (the same floor stores, of b)
own.escape std::gpu::wgsl::msl::write_entry  sound: push_fmt/push_str into w.out copy the bytes (the same floor stores, of in_buf and nb)
own.escape std::gpu::wgsl::msl::zero_workgroup  sound: push_fmt of lv into w.out copies the bytes (the same floor stores, of b)
